 ## Overview
-Farthest Point Sampling Initialization is a method for selecting a subset of points from a point cloud such that they are maximally spread out in Euclidean space, ensuring maximum spatial coverage [S1][S2, unofficial]. It serves as the primary initialization step for primitive positions in neural rendering representations, replacing simpler nearest-neighbor heuristics to prevent the formation of overly small primitives [S1]. It implements the iterative selection logic and CUDA-optimized kernel calls required to generate the initial set of indices [S2, unofficial].
+Farthest Point Sampling Initialization is a method for selecting a subset of points from a point cloud such that they are maximally spread out in Euclidean space, ensuring maximum spatial coverage [S1][S2, unofficial]. It serves as the primary initialization step for primitive positions in neural rendering representations, replacing simpler nearest-neighbor heuristics to prevent the formation of overly small primitives [S1]. It implements the iterative selection logic and CUDA-optimized kernel calls required to generate the initial set of indices [S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Farthest Point Sampling (FPS)](7182-farthest-point-sampling-fps.md) by applying the iterative farthest-point selection strategy specifically to initialize primitive positions.
 
